anya-cs: Heads-up — acme corp seeing intermittent 429s during SDK onboarding. Started ~10:05am PST after we rolled ephemeral keys. Logs show repeated preflight calls from browser workers.

devon-eng: Can you paste a raw request/response snippet? Also which SDK (browser/node) and version?

anya-cs: Browser SDK v0.12.4. Snip:

> Request: GET /v1/preflight
> Headers: Authorization: Bearer eyJ..., x-client-id: acme-123
> Response: 429, body: {"error":"rate_limited"}, headers: {"Retry-After":"1"}

anya-cs: Noticed many clients doing simultaneous token refresh every 60s. Their code sets refresh interval to 60 and no jitter.

devon-eng: Ah — thundering herd. Recommend adding splay/jitter + exponential backoff. Also set local ephemeral token cache TTL > jitter window so preflight coalesces.

mike-sre: For now, rate limit policy: edge returns Retry-After in seconds; SDK should respect it. Suggest server-side mitigation too: increase preflight cache to 120s for this tenant and enable small sliding window dedupe.

devon-eng: Quick patch we can tell them to try (browser JS):

```js
// add jitter + exp backoff
async function refreshToken() {
  let base = 1000;
  for (let i=0;i<5;i++) {
    try { return await fetch('/auth/refresh'); }
    catch(e) { await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, base * Math.pow(2,i) * (0.8 + Math.random()*0.4))); }
  }
}
```

anya-cs: I'll send that to them. Also asking them to upgrade to v0.12.6 (fixes preflight dedupe bug). Will schedule a quick join at 2pm PST.

ratebot: alert — tenant=acme-corp peak_429_rate=37/min window=60s

devon-eng: Perfect. If they still spike after client patch, we'll temporarily bump their preflight cache on the gateway and roll a canary with increased token TTL for 10 mins.

anya-cs: thanks — I'll coordinate and post results here. :thumbsup:
